  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.0",
    "value": "The same observed directed topology and unchanged SUMO vehicle/junction parameters are used in every comparison; the microscopic model is not calibrated field truth."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.1",
    "value": "The six original OD release schedules are independent of the number of candidate routes. All request IDs, original release times and vehicle properties are fixed within paired groups."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.2",
    "value": "A selects a same-endpoint candidate at release using current known external-edge speed costs. The default participates, ties retain default, and future event recovery or future tasks are not consulted."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.3",
    "value": "B adds bounded source admission after task publication. It acts only on ordinary requests released at/after the task and not yet submitted to SUMO whose chosen path intersects the task's currently remaining corridor."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.4",
    "value": "Task corridor updates use current TraCI vehicle route position; before task insertion its already assigned route is used. Each ordinary request waits at most 45 seconds at source, and task-related control expires 180 seconds after release."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.5",
    "value": "Source admission authority is an explicit hypothetical governance action. All source control and SUMO insertion waiting remain charged from the unchanged original release time."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.6",
    "value": "Task and ordinary vehicles share exactly one vType and the same road permissions. There is no special speed, red-light override, lane priority, repositioning or vehicle removal."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.7",
    "value": "Slow-event speeds and durations are predeclared assumptions, not observed accidents or measured capacity. All profile results, including no benefit or harm, are retained."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.8",
    "value": "The fixed experiment anchor maps simulation seconds to a declared wall clock only; the counterfactual traffic demand and event are not a reconstruction of the live collection window."
  },
  {
    "file": "config/final_experiments.json",
    "field": "assumptions.9",
    "value": "A fitted ETA observation layer, if supplied separately, is a statistical reference and does not identify or validate the microscopic parameters."
  },
